    {
      "name": "the-safe-dial",
      "type": "registry:block",
      "title": "The Safe Dial",
      "description": "A combination dial in SVG, the lock face of a vault bolted to the bench. One number is the dial's angle: the knurled rim and its graduations turn under a fixed index, the readout fills as the three numbers of the combination land in order, and the bolt throws back through the plate the moment it is right. Nothing is cut away, and the bolt is the only part that moves through the solid plate. It runs its own loop with a play/pause control, and once paused you can spin the dial or drive it with the arrow keys.",
      "categories": [
        "svg",
        "isometric",
